 r←Test_AskNumber_006(stopFlag batchFlag);parms;was;msg;n;⎕TRAP
⍝ Exercise the "OnOkay" callback with all possible ways to define it.
 r←∆Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP'
 #.TEMP←⎕NS''
 #.TEMP.MyCallback←{
     n←⍵
     1<n.Input.Value:1
     n.StatusField1.Text←'Too low'
     n.StatusField1.BCol←n.∆globalParms.alarmColor
     0
 }
 #.TEMP.parms←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Request.CreateParmsForNumber
 #.TEMP.parms.value←1
 #.TEMP.parms.timeout←0.1
 #.TEMP.parms.onOkay←'#.TEMP.MyCallback'

 n←#.TEMP.parms(#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Request.CreateParmsForNumber ∆Ask)'Number of copies:'
 2 ∆Process n.∆Form
 →GoToTidyUp n.StatusField1.Text≢'Too low'
 n.Input ∆KeyPress'4'
 ⎕NQ n.Input 9995
 ∆Process n.∆Form
 ⎕NQ n.Btn0'Select'
 ∆Process n.∆Form
 →FailsIf 4≢n.∆result
 r←∆OK

∆TidyUp:
 n.∆CloseForm
